{
  "id": "p7",
  "title": "Procedures",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "p7-l1",
      "title": "Your Own Procedure",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A procedure is a named piece of program. You write it once, above the main begin, and then call it by its name as often as you like.",
        "procedure Line; begin writeln('----------'); end; Calling Line; runs those statements. Note the ; after the procedure's end.",
        "This was Wirth's big idea: build programs from small, named blocks that each do one job."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Banner;",
          "",
          "procedure Line;",
          "begin",
          "  writeln('--------------');",
          "end;",
          "",
          "begin",
          "  Line;",
          "  writeln(' TURBO PASCAL');",
          "  Line;",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "--------------",
          " TURBO PASCAL",
          "--------------"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p7-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Where is a procedure declared?",
          "options": [
            "Above the main begin",
            "After end.",
            "Inside writeln",
            "Anywhere in the main block"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Like variables, procedures are declared before they are used."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How do you run a procedure called Beep?",
          "options": [
            "Beep;",
            "call Beep;",
            "Beep();;",
            "run Beep;"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Just its name (brackets are optional when it has no parameters)."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l1-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Twice;",
            "",
            "procedure Hello;",
            "begin",
            "  writeln('Hi');",
            "end;",
            "",
            "begin",
            "  Hello;",
            "  Hello;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "Hi\nHi",
            "Hi",
            "nothing",
            "Hello"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Hello is called twice."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l1-e4",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Finish the procedure.",
          "code": [
            "___ Stars;",
            "begin",
            "  writeln('*****');",
            "end;"
          ],
          "options": [
            "procedure",
            "function",
            "program",
            "void"
          ],
          "answer": "procedure",
          "explanation": "A procedure starts with the word procedure."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l1-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program P;",
            "",
            "procedure Greet;",
            "begin",
            "  writeln('Hello');",
            "end",
            "",
            "begin",
            "  Greet;",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 5,
          "explanation": "A procedure's end is followed by a semicolon: end;"
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why use procedures?",
          "options": [
            "To write a job once and reuse it, and to keep programs readable",
            "Because Pascal can't run without them",
            "They make programs run faster",
            "To hide errors"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Small named pieces are easier to understand and fix."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p7-l2",
      "title": "Parameters",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Parameters make a procedure flexible: procedure Line(n: integer); gets a number from the caller. Line(5) runs it with n = 5.",
        "Several parameters are separated by semicolons in the declaration (n: integer; c: char) and by commas in the call: Line(10, '=').",
        "These value parameters are copies: changing n inside the procedure doesn't change anything outside."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Lines;",
          "",
          "procedure Line(n: integer; c: char);",
          "var",
          "  i: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  for i := 1 to n do",
          "    write(c);",
          "  writeln;",
          "end;",
          "",
          "begin",
          "  Line(10, '=');",
          "  Line(4, '*');",
          "  Line(10, '=');",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "==========",
          "****",
          "=========="
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p7-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How do you call procedure Box(w, h: integer) with 3 and 4?",
          "options": [
            "Box(3, 4);",
            "Box(3; 4);",
            "Box 3, 4;",
            "Box[3, 4];"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Commas between the values in the call."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program R;",
            "",
            "procedure Row(n: integer);",
            "var",
            "  i: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for i := 1 to n do",
            "    write('#');",
            "  writeln;",
            "end;",
            "",
            "begin",
            "  Row(6);",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "######",
            "6",
            "#",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Row prints n characters."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l2-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Declare two parameters of different types.",
          "code": [
            "procedure Show(n: integer___ c: char);"
          ],
          "options": [
            ";",
            ",",
            ":",
            "and"
          ],
          "answer": ";",
          "explanation": "In the declaration, groups of parameters are separated by semicolons."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l2-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Copy;",
            "var",
            "  x: integer;",
            "",
            "procedure Bump(n: integer);",
            "begin",
            "  n := n + 1;",
            "end;",
            "",
            "begin",
            "  x := 5;",
            "  Bump(x);",
            "  writeln(x);",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "5",
            "6",
            "an error",
            "0"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "n is a copy. Adding 1 inside Bump doesn't change x."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l2-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Call;",
            "",
            "procedure Repeat3(c: char);",
            "begin",
            "  writeln(c, c, c);",
            "end;",
            "",
            "begin",
            "  Repeat3('a', 'b');",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 8,
          "explanation": "Repeat3 has one parameter, but gets two values."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l2-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is a value parameter?",
          "options": [
            "A copy of the value the caller passes",
            "A link to the caller's variable",
            "A global variable",
            "A constant"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Changes to it stay inside the procedure."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p7-l3",
      "title": "Local Variables",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Variables declared inside a procedure are local: they exist only while it runs, and nothing outside can see them. Two procedures can each have their own i.",
        "Global variables, declared at the top of the program, are visible everywhere. Use them sparingly: when every procedure can change them, mistakes are hard to find.",
        "In Turbo Pascal, local variables are not set to 0: they start with whatever was left in memory. Always give them a value first."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Scope;",
          "var",
          "  calls: integer;",
          "",
          "procedure Count;",
          "var",
          "  i, total: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  total := 0;",
          "  for i := 1 to 4 do",
          "    total := total + i;",
          "  writeln('Local total: ', total);",
          "end;",
          "",
          "begin",
          "  calls := 0;",
          "  Count;",
          "  calls := calls + 1;",
          "  Count;",
          "  calls := calls + 1;",
          "  writeln('Count ran ', calls, ' times');",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "Local total: 10",
          "Local total: 10",
          "Count ran 2 times"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p7-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Where can a local variable be used?",
          "options": [
            "Only inside its procedure",
            "Everywhere",
            "Only in the main program",
            "Only after the procedure ran"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "It exists only while the procedure runs."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What value does a local integer have before you set it?",
          "options": [
            "Whatever was left in memory",
            "Always 0",
            "Always 1",
            "It's an error to declare it"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Globals start at 0 in Turbo Pascal, locals don't."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l3-e3",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This procedure prints a strange number. Which line is missing?",
          "code": [
            "procedure Sum;",
            "var",
            "  i, s: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for i := 1 to 3 do",
            "    s := s + i;",
            "  writeln(s);",
            "end;"
          ],
          "answer": 4,
          "explanation": "s needs s := 0; before the loop. As a local variable, it starts with leftover garbage."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l3-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Can two procedures both have a local variable called i?",
          "options": [
            "Yes, each one has its own",
            "No, names must be unique in the program",
            "Only if they have the same type",
            "Only in Turbo Pascal 3"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Locals belong to their procedure."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l3-e5",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Give the procedure its own counter.",
          "code": [
            "procedure Countdown;",
            "___",
            "  k: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for k := 3 downto 1 do",
            "    write(k, ' ');",
            "end;"
          ],
          "options": [
            "var",
            "local",
            "const",
            "begin"
          ],
          "answer": "var",
          "explanation": "A procedure can have its own var section."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7-l3-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why should you use few global variables?",
          "options": [
            "Any procedure could change them, which makes mistakes hard to find",
            "They are slower",
            "Pascal only allows five",
            "They use more disk space"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Parameters and locals keep each procedure independent."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
